   "args": {
    "text": "Verdict: not supported\n\nOlah et al. (2020) supports the polysemanticity part: it says neural networks often contain neurons responding to multiple unrelated inputs and gives an InceptionV1 neuron responding to cat faces, car fronts, and cat legs as an example. It also documents interpretable neuron examples such as curve detectors, so it is consistent with the claim that neuron-based analysis has had some success. (distill:zoom-in/r1/b27; distill:zoom-in/r1/b62)\n\nBut I could not verify the combined citation for “some success” against Bills et al. (2023): the library search did not return that cited work as a document. The available Olah source supports the sentence’s account of polysemantic neurons; it does not by itself establish what Bills et al. showed."
   },
   "returned": [],
