   "kind": "answer",
   "delta": "Verdict: not supported\n\nOlah et al. (2020) supports the claim about polysemantic neurons: it describes neurons that respond to multiple unrelated inputs and gives the example of one InceptionV1 neuron responding to cat faces, car fronts, and cat legs. It also describes curve detecting neurons, consistent with neuron based analysis having some success. (distill:zoom-in/r1/b27; distill:zoom-in/r1/b62)\n\nHowever, I could not verify the “some success” claim against Bills et al. (2023): the library search did not return that cited work as a document. The available Olah source supports the polysemanticity claim, but it cannot establish what Bills et al. showed."
